shing\nINFO  2026-10-17T07:04:42 +0ms service=bus type=storage.write publishing\nINFO  2026-10-17T07:04:42 +0ms service=bus type=message.updated publishing\nINFO  2026-10-17T07:04:42 +0ms service=session session=ses_eb752e9ccffe7J9cBMLq8WERq3 type=finish part\nINFO  2026-10-17T07:04:42 +1ms service=bus type=storage.write publishing\nINFO  2026-10-17T07:04:42 +0ms service=bus type=message.updated publishing\nINFO  2026-10-17T07:04:42 +5ms service=bus type=storage.write publishing\nINFO  2026-10-17T07:04:42 +0ms service=bus type=message.updated publishing\nINFO  2026-10-17T07:04:42 +0ms service=session session=ses_eb752e9ccffe7J9cBMLq8WERq3 sessionID=ses_eb752e9ccffe7J9cBMLq8WERq3 unlocking\nINFO  2026-10-17T07:04:42 +0ms service=bus type=session.idle publishing\nI fixed six bugs in `catalog/`, but I couldn't run `python3 -m unittest`. I have no shell in this session, so none of the fixes have been run against the suite. I checked each fix by reading it against the tests.\n\n- **`fees.py`:** the late fee added the daily rate to the days late instead of multiplying (`+` changed to `*`).\n- **`members.py`:** `MAX_BORROWED` was 3. The tests and the policy comment both say 5.\n- **`inventory.py`:** `recent(n)` returned `n + 1` events. It now returns the last `n`, or an empty list when `n` is 0 or less.\n- **`factory.py`:** `sample_books()` was missing `Emma`. I added it as `Book(\"Emma\", \"Austen\", 1815, 1)`. The author, year and copies are my choice, since the tests only check the title.\n- **`books.py`:** `parse_book` left the year as a string. It now converts it with `int()`.\n- **`search.py`:** it imported `normalize` from `catalog.nonexistent`. It now imports it from `catalog.text`.\n\nPlease run `python3 -m unittest` to confirm.INFO  2026-10-17T07:04:42 +0ms service=app name=lsp shutdown\nINFO  2026-10-17T07:04:42 +0ms service=app name=session shutdown\nINFO  2026-10-17T07:04:42 +0ms service=app name=mcp shutdown\n", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "pa